   'Otis honors U.S. Marine Lt. Col. Christopher "Otis" Raible, 40, of North Huntington, Pennsylvania, the commanding officer of Marine Attack Squadron 211. He was killed by insurgents during an attack on Camp Bastion, Afghanistan, on Sept. 14, 2012. He trained CrossFit with his family, and his favorite movements included deadlifts, squats and overhead presses.

For 15 minutes you climb a ladder of three lifts: 1 back squat, 1 shoulder press and 1 deadlift, then 2 of each, then 3 of each, and so on. The squats and deadlifts use 1½ times your body weight and the press uses ¾ of your body weight. The loads are heavy from the first rep, and every rung adds a rep, so the sets get long fast.',
   '[{"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "1, 2, 3, ... (add 1 each round)", "tip": "Bar on your upper back, brace hard and squat below parallel before you stand.", "rx_men": "1½ x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1½ x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Overhead Press", "reps": "1, 2, 3, ... (add 1 each round)", "tip": "This is a strict shoulder press: no dip or leg drive. Press the bar straight up and lock out with your head through.", "rx_men": "¾ x bodyweight", "rx_women": "¾ x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "1, 2, 3, ... (add 1 each round)", "tip": "Set a flat back before every pull and push the floor away.", "rx_men": "1½ x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1½ x bodyweight"}]'::jsonb,
