   'Owen honors Petty Officer Owen Green of the Royal Navy, who died on June 3, 2026, during a routine training exercise. He achieved his goal of joining the armed forces in 2022 and completed an Arctic expedition during his service.

You complete 5 rounds of 24 back squats with a barbell loaded to your own body weight, followed by an 800 m run. That is 120 heavy squats and 4,000 m of running. The squats tire your legs before every run, and the runs leave little time to recover before the next barbell set.',
   '[{"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "24", "tip": "Bar on your upper back, chest up, squat below parallel. Break the set before your form slips.", "rx_men": "Bodyweight", "rx_women": "Bodyweight"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Settle into a steady pace. Your legs will feel heavy for the first 200 m."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
