You complete 7 rounds of 11 deficit handstand push-ups and a 1,000 m run. That is 77 deficit handstand push-ups and 7 km of running. The deficit makes each push-up deeper and harder than a standard rep, and the long runs mean this one takes a while. CrossFit does not set a deficit height, so pick one and use it every round.',
   '[{"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "11 (deficit)", "tip": "Put your hands on plates or parallettes so your head drops below hand level. Lower under control and press to lockout."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you can repeat seven times. Shake your arms out as you go."}]'::jsonb,
