   'Pat honors Army Sgt. Patrick Hawkins, 25, of Carlisle, Pennsylvania, assigned to the 3rd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment of Fort Benning, Georgia. He was killed on Oct. 6, 2013, during a special operations mission in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan. He often trained CrossFit with his Fire Team.

You run 800 m carrying a 25 lb plate, then complete 14 rounds of 5 strict pull-ups, 4 burpee box jumps (24 in / 20 in) and 3 cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), then finish with another 800 m plate run. CrossFit does not say how to hold the plate or which clean to use, so any clean counts. The heavy cleans and strict pull-ups add up across 14 rounds.',
   '[{"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold the plate however works for you: at your chest, overhead, or switching as you go.", "rx_men": "25 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "5 (14 rounds)", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jumps", "reps": "4 (14 rounds)", "tip": "Chest to the floor, stand, then jump onto the box and stand tall on top.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Cleans", "reps": "3 (14 rounds)", "tip": "Any clean counts. Quick singles keep your back safe at this load.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "The last effort. Hold the plate the same way you found worked on the first run.", "rx_men": "25 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
