   'Peyton honors Chad Robert Peyton, a U.S. Army veteran with 10 years of military service who rose to the rank of Captain and flew UH-60 Black Hawk helicopters. He struggled with depression and anxiety, and he took his own life on May 17, 2021. He was a beloved member of the CrossFit community in Santa Cruz, California.

For 20 minutes you do as many rounds as possible of 10 chest-to-bar pull-ups and 10 dumbbell thrusters (50 lb / 35 lb). Every 2 minutes, starting at 0:00, you stop and do 40 double-unders. At the 20:00 mark you finish with a 2-mile run. If you or someone you know is struggling, call or text 988 (Veterans: press 1).',
   '[{"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "40 every 2:00, starting at 0:00", "tip": "Stop where you are and do these on each 2-minute mark, then go back to the round."}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Kipping is fine."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Thrusters", "reps": "10", "tip": "Front squat to a press in one motion. Drive with your legs to move the dumbbells.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "2 miles, at 20:00", "tip": "Start right when the AMRAP ends. Find a steady pace and hold it."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps of the 20-minute AMRAP. CrossFit does not say how to score the 2-mile run, so record your run time as well.',
   '["Do the double-unders the moment each 2-minute mark hits", "Break the chest-to-bars early", "Save something for the 2-mile run"]'::jsonb,
   '["Keep your rope next to the pull-up bar so you can grab it right on the 2-minute mark.", "Remember where you stopped in the round and pick up from there after the double-unders.", "Break the chest-to-bar pull-ups into sets of 5 before your grip fades.", "On the thrusters, keep your elbows high in the squat so the dumbbells stay on your shoulders.", "Start the run gently and settle in, because 2 miles is long after 20 hard minutes."]'::jsonb,
