   'Pheezy honors U.S. Marine Corps Lance Cpl. Philip P. Clark, 19, of Gainesville, Florida, assigned to 1st Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment, 2nd Marine Division, II Marine Expeditionary Force at Camp Lejeune, North Carolina. He died on May 18, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan.

You complete 3 rounds of 5 front squats (165 lb / 115 lb), 18 pull-ups, 5 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), 18 toes-to-bar, 5 push jerks (165 lb / 115 lb) and 18 hand-release push-ups. Heavy barbell sets alternate with high-rep gymnastics, so your grip and core stay busy the whole way.',
   '[{"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "5", "tip": "Elbows high, chest up, squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "165 lb", "rx_women": "115 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "18", "tip": "Chin clears the bar on every rep. Break into sets before your grip fails."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "5", "tip": "Flat back, bar close, stand all the way up.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "18", "tip": "Kick your toes to touch the bar between your hands."}, {"name": "Push Jerks", "reps": "5", "tip": "Dip and drive, then push under the bar and lock out overhead.", "rx_men": "165 lb", "rx_women": "115 lb"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "18", "tip": "Chest and thighs touch the floor, lift your hands, then press back up."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
