   '[{"question": "What is the Pheezy workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of 5 front squats (165 lb / 115 lb), 18 pull-ups, 5 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), 18 toes-to-bar, 5 push jerks (165 lb / 115 lb) and 18 hand-release push-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Pheezy?", "answer": "207 reps: 15 front squats, 54 pull-ups, 15 deadlifts, 54 toes-to-bar, 15 push jerks and 54 hand-release push-ups."}, {"question": "Do I need two barbells?", "answer": "It helps. The deadlift is heavier than the front squats and push jerks, so a second bar saves you from changing plates."}, {"question": "Who was Pheezy?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Corps Lance Cpl. Philip P. Clark, 19, of Gainesville, Florida, of the 1st Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment. He died on May 18, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
