   'Pikey honors Master Sgt. William "Pikey" Posch, 36, an 18-year Air Force veteran and pararescueman with the Air Force Reserve''s 308th Rescue Squadron at Patrick Air Force Base, Florida. He died on March 15, 2018, when an HH-60 Pave Hawk helicopter crashed in the Anbar Province of Iraq. He was a member of CrossFit JAX and loved running and bodyweight movements.

This chipper alternates runs with 12 burpee bar muscle-ups and a barbell set: 15 squat snatches, then 20 clean and jerks, then 18 thrusters. The runs go 400 m, 800 m, 800 m and 400 m. One 155 lb / 105 lb bar is used for all three lifts, and the snatches come first while you are fresh.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Start easy. There is a lot of work after this."}, {"name": "Burpee Bar Muscle-Ups", "reps": "12", "tip": "Burpee, jump to the bar and do a bar muscle-up. Every rep starts with your chest on the floor."}, {"name": "Squat Snatches", "reps": "15", "tip": "Catch the bar in a full overhead squat. Quick singles are fine.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Steady pace. Shake your arms out."}, {"name": "Burpee Bar Muscle-Ups", "reps": "12", "tip": "Keep a steady rhythm rather than rushing the first few."}, {"name": "Clean and Jerks", "reps": "20", "tip": "Any clean and any jerk count. Singles keep your back safe.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold the same pace as the last 800 m."}, {"name": "Burpee Bar Muscle-Ups", "reps": "12", "tip": "The last set. Break it up if your grip is tired."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "18", "tip": "Front squat to a press in one motion. Use your legs to drive the bar.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Finish strong."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
