   'Lower the barbell to 95 lb / 65 lb or less. Use power snatches or hang power snatches if the squat snatch is not there yet. Replace burpee bar muscle-ups with burpee pull-ups or burpees and jumping pull-ups. Cut every set in half for a shorter version.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Pikey workout?", "answer": "For time: run 400 m, 12 burpee bar muscle-ups, 15 squat snatches, run 800 m, 12 burpee bar muscle-ups, 20 clean and jerks, run 800 m, 12 burpee bar muscle-ups, 18 thrusters, run 400 m. The barbell is 155 lb / 105 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Pikey?", "answer": "89 reps: 36 burpee bar muscle-ups, 15 squat snatches, 20 clean and jerks and 18 thrusters, plus 2,400 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Pikey?", "answer": "Master Sgt. William \"Pikey\" Posch, 36, a pararescueman with the Air Force Reserve''s 308th Rescue Squadron. He died on March 15, 2018, when an HH-60 Pave Hawk helicopter crashed in the Anbar Province of Iraq."}, {"question": "What is a burpee bar muscle-up?", "answer": "A burpee followed by a jump to the pull-up bar and a bar muscle-up, finishing with your arms locked out above the bar."}]'::jsonb,
