You complete 5 rounds of 10 back squats (225 lb / 155 lb), 10 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb) and a 400 m sprint, with 2 minutes of rest between rounds. The loads are heavy and the run is a sprint, so your legs get very little relief. CrossFit does not say whether the rest counts toward your time, so note how you scored it.',
   '[{"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "10", "tip": "Squat from a rack. Brace hard and squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "10", "tip": "Flat back, bar close, push the floor away.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "This is a sprint, not a jog. Drive your arms."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Rest 2 minutes between rounds."}]'::jsonb,
