You complete 5 rounds of a 400 m run, 7 strict pull-ups, 7 strict handstand push-ups, 20 toes-to-bar, 22 alternating dumbbell snatches (50 lb / 35 lb) and a 200 m dumbbell carry. CrossFit does not say whether to carry one dumbbell or two, or how to hold it, so note your choice. Strict gymnastics and long dumbbell work make each round long.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold a steady pace you can repeat for five rounds."}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Strict Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "No kip. Lower your head to the floor under control and press to lockout."}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "20", "tip": "Kick your toes to touch the bar between your hands."}, {"name": "Alternating Dumbbell Snatches", "reps": "22", "tip": "Switch hands every rep and lock out overhead.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Dumbbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "CrossFit says only dumbbell carry. Carry it however you choose and use the same style every round.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}]'::jsonb,
